# Maintain agent docs (ctrim_app)

After completing work, check whether agent guidance needs updating. Use skill `maintain-agent-docs` for the full checklist.

## Update when

- New architectural pattern (manager type, state holder, test layout, new `lib/pages/` area)
- Cross-cutting behavior change (auth, Firestore access, info/Quill, web debug)
- Non-obvious bug fix a future agent would hit again
- New dependency or command agents should know about

## Skip when

- Routine bugfixes, typos, styling, or one-off changes with no reusable lesson

## Where to edit

| Change type | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| Always-on conventions | `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` |
| Workflow / domain how-to | `.cursor/skills/<name>/` |
| Quick orientation + changelog | `AGENTS.md` (Recent changes section) |
| Copilot / cloud agents | `.github/copilot-instructions.md` |

Keep edits minimal. Add a one-line entry to `AGENTS.md` → **Recent agent-relevant changes**. Do not commit doc-only updates unless the user asks.
